> 1.) Is it possible to only sip at a potion before swallowing the
> whole? 

No, you can only quaff the whole bottle.

> I'm thinking of testing for poison for example or already 
> getting this typical mesage, that lets me guess, what this potion is.
> If not so: Is there a way of identifying potion without scroll of
> identify without swallowing or throwing at monsters?

Poison --that is, the potion of sickness-- *can* be identified: dip some
darts or arrows in, and if "the potion forms a coating on the darts"
you'll know it's sickness and your darts or arrows will be poisoned. (I
usually throw them away or sell them after that, because I don't use
poison on principle, but that's just me). It does use up one potion.

Potions of water are always clear. 

Dipping a unicorn horn into some potions that are bad for you will turn
them into water. You'll know that the potion you dipped into was bad for
you, but not what it was.

Dipping an amethyst stone into booze turns it into fruit juice. (This is
also useful to tell your violet gems apart if you have known booze)

> 2.) Is it possible to mix potions? 

Yes. This is called alchemy and there's a spoiler about it.

